[sub_resource type="BoxShape3D" id="Shape_stand"]
size = Vector3(0.6, 1.1, 0.6)

; 38Q, Bryn's order bench. prp_table_large has NO node scale and root_scale 1.0, so its 2.848 x
; 0.813 x 1.097 is the real size — the same measurement embermarket.tscn records for Nessa's assay
; counter, and this reuses the number rather than re-deriving it. ⚠️ 38P2's trap is that a measured
; box is fiction until node scale and nodes/root_scale are applied; both are 1 here and were checked.
;
; ⚠️ prp_weapon_stand was authored here FIRST and rejected on the render — fifth time this trap has
; fired. A smith's empty weapon rack is the right idea and the wrong object: from any side but
; straight-on the slots are invisible and it reads as a SAWHORSE, so the prompt would be inviting the
; player to commission a sword from a trestle. Nothing in the .tscn or the filename said so.
[sub_resource type="BoxShape3D" id="Shape_order_bench"]
size = Vector3(2.848, 0.813, 1.097)

; The cottage's own collider, sized to bld_cottage.glb (4.84 x 4.20 x 4.70). It is NOT Shape_bldgA:
; that box is the two-storey town house's, and a collider a metre and a half taller than the roof
; it guards is a wall the player bumps into before reaching the building.

[sub_resource type="BoxShape3D" id="Shape_cottage"]
size = Vector3(4.84, 4.2, 4.7)

; The square used two models at four mounts, which reads as a copied asset rather than a village.
; The inn and the smithy give the innkeeper and the Warband's smith buildings to stand in front of.

[sub_resource type="BoxShape3D" id="Shape_inn"]
size = Vector3(8.66, 7.5, 8.64)

