; --- 37D: the Ashfall Cottage itself ------------------------------------------
; Until 37D the "cottage" was BuildingSW — a generic greybox town house shared with the 27B square,
; with the deed post and the stash bolted to its outside wall. It now has its own building in the
; south-west corner, clear of BuildingSW (footprint x -16..-8, z -25..-19), with a walled room in
; front of it holding the stash and the trophy stands.
;
; EVERYTHING HERE PARENTS TO Nav. Geometry outside the NavigationRegion3D is not carved into the
; bake (27A), so walls parented to the cell root would leave every NPC and enemy pathing straight
; through the cottage — visible only as actors walking through walls, which reads as a nav bug
; anywhere but here.
;
; Room interior spans x -26..-18, z -22.5..-16.5, with a 2.5 m doorway in the north wall facing the
; square. Roofless by design: an enterable interior needs a scene transition convention this repo
; does not have yet, and inventing one here would pre-empt the Phase 44 region work that owns it.

; ⚠️ THE MODEL CHILD CARRIES A COUNTER-OFFSET. The building node sits at half its own height so the
; box collider (which is centred on its origin) spans ground to roof; the .glb's origin is at its
; BASE, so without -Y on the Model the house hangs in the air by half its height. Every other
; building here does this (BuildingNW/NE -3.75, BuildingSW/SE -3.4) and the first cut of this node
; did not — a cottage floating 3.75 m over its own garden.

[node name="Cottage" type="MeshInstance3D" parent="Nav"]
transform = Transform3D(1, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 1, -22, 2.1, -25.35)

[node name="CottageCol" type="StaticBody3D" parent="Nav/Cottage"]

[node name="Shape" type="CollisionShape3D" parent="Nav/Cottage/CottageCol"]
shape = SubResource("Shape_cottage")

[node name="Model" parent="Nav/Cottage" instance=ExtResource("36_cottage")]
transform = Transform3D(1, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, -2.1, 0)

